#: passwords.cpp:48
msgid "Echo characters as"
msgstr "Eĥu pasvorton kiel"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid ""
"Here you can configure the visual feedback given when you have to enter a "
"password in kdesu. It does not affect other programs.<p> You can chose "
"between: <ul><li><em>1 star:</em> for each character entered, an asterisk "
"(*) appears.</li><li><em>3 stars:</em> for each character entered, three "
"asterisks appear.</li> <li><em>no echo:</em> you don't get any visual feed "
"back (so people watching can't even tell how many characters your password "
"has).</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: passwords.cpp:58
msgid "1 star"
msgstr "unu steleto"

#: passwords.cpp:60
msgid "3 stars"
msgstr "tri steletoj"

#: passwords.cpp:62
msgid "no echo"
msgstr "sen eĥo"

#: passwords.cpp:68
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "&Memoru la pasvortojn"

#: passwords.cpp:69
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, kdesu will remember your passwords for a given "
"time. This way you don't have to enter your password again everytime you do "
"something that requires a password. Keep in mind that this option is "
"insecure and may enable others to do harm to your information and your "
"system.<p> Please <em>do not</em> use this option if you are working in an "
"insecure environment (e.g. in an open-plan office).<p> This option does not "
"affect passwords explicitely set in applications, e.g. your mail password in "
"KMail."
msgstr ""

#: passwords.cpp:80
msgid "&Timeout"
msgstr "&Tempolimo"

#: passwords.cpp:85
msgid ""
"Here you can specify for how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A "
"short timeout is more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"Tie ĉi vi povas difini, kiom longe KDEsu memoru viajn pasvortojn."
"Mallonga tempolimo estas pli sekura ol longa."

#: passwords.cpp:92
msgid " minutes"
msgstr " minutoj"

#: passwords.cpp:205
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> For some actions, like changing the date/time of your "
"system clock or creating users on your system, you need special privileges. "
"In these cases a KDE program called 'kdesu' will ask you for a password. "
"Here you can configure the behavior of kdesu, i.e. what visual feedback is "
"given when you enter a password and whether kdesu should remember your "
"passwords for a certain time.<p> These settings affect kdesu <em>only</em>. "
"This means that e.g. the behavior of KMail and other programs asking you for "
"passwords can not be configured here."
msgstr ""

